From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lun Dong <lundong@google.com>
Date: Fri, 10 Oct 2026 00:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Speed up Zvt matmul, RVV and dispatch emulation

Emulation overhead dominated the simulator wall time of matmul-heavy
workloads. Results are bit-identical:
- RiscVZvtMatmul reads each operand element and punning offset once
  instead of once per multiply-accumulate (one vtfmm was ~25x slower
  to emulate than a vector instruction).
- Unmasked vector loads, stores and element-wise ops with vstart == 0
  write straight to the register buffers.
- RiscVTop skips advancing the delay lines while the function and data
  buffer ones are empty, and keeps a decode cache per ITCM .text image
  across dispatches.
- RVLoad keeps its LoadContext on the stack.
---
